        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "General solvothermal/sonochemical preparation of Ln12(HL)6(L)6(NO3)6·xH2O: 2,3-dihydroxybenzoic acid (77.0 mg, 0.5 mmol) and Ln(NO3)3·6H2O (2.0 mmol) were dissolved in 1 mL high-purity water and 1.5 mL anhydrous methanol; 60 μL triethylamine was slowly added under ultrasound at room temperature. The mixture was sonicated for 10 h, then heated at 105 °C for four days. Colorless block-shaped crystals of 1 were obtained after cooling. Yield 37% based on Sm.",
